(6408461, 949355, 63218, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the info included in comments, I read it with interest. Also the camera settings. A flower show usually has surprisingly awful lighting &amp; I think it goes un-noticed because our sight can compensate so well for it. Something only a photog would know! This one stood out for me during voting for the combination of low light and color clarity, so I was doubly glad you included PP comments. The square crop works well w/this. I guess it depends on the computer''s power but I have learned to crop last. If the image is PP &amp; saved before cropping then I have something to work with if I need a different crop.  I have tried to duplicate my PP on the same image so I can crop differently, but I have never been able to do it. Which is wierd, but I have read the same comment from others. Anyway, good job!</td>', 'Thanks for the info included in comments, I read it with interest. Also the camera settings. A flower show usually has surprisingly awful lighting & I think it goes un-noticed because our sight can compensate so well for it. Something only a photog would know! This one stood out for me during voting for the combination of low light and color clarity, so I was doubly glad you included PP comments. The square crop works well w/this. I guess it depends on the computer''s power but I have learned to crop last. If the image is PP & saved before cropping then I have something to work with if I need a different crop.  I have tried to duplicate my PP on the same image so I can crop differently, but I have never been able to do it. Which is wierd, but I have read the same comment from others. Anyway, good job!', '2011-05-09 11:03:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6408467, 949440, 63218, '<td valign="top">I''ve been following your flower shots since before I joined this site. It has been interesting to appreciate your choice of BG/context for your flowers, &amp; the way you use the light. I keep thinking I can recognize your work during voting, but you keep surprising me. So, thanks!</td>', 'I''ve been following your flower shots since before I joined this site. It has been interesting to appreciate your choice of BG/context for your flowers, & the way you use the light. I keep thinking I can recognize your work during voting, but you keep surprising me. So, thanks!', '2011-05-09 11:13:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6408468, 948670, 11518, '<td valign="top">This should have been on the front page!!!!</td>', 'This should have been on the front page!!!!', '2011-05-09 11:19:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6408469, 949149, 67152, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot and great finish.  I was so wanting to go visit my friends the owls up in Vermont, but I couldn''t find the time.  This shot is wonderful and the details throughout are first rate.  I had to ''settle'' for some cattle instead!</td>', 'Excellent shot and great finish.  I was so wanting to go visit my friends the owls up in Vermont, but I couldn''t find the time.  This shot is wonderful and the details throughout are first rate.  I had to ''settle'' for some cattle instead!', '2011-05-09 11:23:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6408471, 949149, 54446, '<td valign="top">Degree of difficulty is very low for an image capture of an owl in captivity.  If this owl was not confined by a leather tether, please let me know.   So, you found an owl at a rehab center or zoo or menagerie and you stuck a camera in it''s face.  Excellent closeup, but no environment, no background, no foreground.  My recommendation for improvement is that you mention the name of the hosting facility.  That''s the least you can do.  Congratulations on your top 10 finish.</td>', 'Degree of difficulty is very low for an image capture of an owl in captivity.  If this owl was not confined by a leather tether, please let me know.   So, you found an owl at a rehab center or zoo or menagerie and you stuck a camera in it''s face.  Excellent closeup, but no environment, no background, no foreground.  My recommendation for improvement is that you mention the name of the hosting facility.  That''s the least you can do.  Congratulations on your top 10 finish.', '2011-05-09 11:29:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6408478, 949363, 67152, '<td valign="top">A lovely image and a great finish Angela.  I was one of your 9s.  The placement of the bee in the lower right corner was well chosen</td>', 'A lovely image and a great finish Angela.  I was one of your 9s.  The placement of the bee in the lower right corner was well chosen', '2011-05-09 11:39:57.000000', NULL, 0),
