(6410407, 948541, 72929, '<td valign="top">To crop a perfect square in Photoshop, press c for the crop tool, click anywhere and drag.. then hold the shift key ===&gt; Square crop. You can also use the marquee selection tool (m) and click-drag-hold shift to get a square selection, which you can then (assuming around Photoshop CS2 or newer) move around before choosing Image-&gt;Crop.<br/> <br/>Great image BTW, sorry you took it on the wrong day.</td>', 'To crop a perfect square in Photoshop, press c for the crop tool, click anywhere and drag.. then hold the shift key ===> Square crop. You can also use the marquee selection tool (m) and click-drag-hold shift to get a square selection, which you can then (assuming around Photoshop CS2 or newer) move around before choosing Image->Crop. Great image BTW, sorry you took it on the wrong day.', '2011-05-11 08:35:18.000000', NULL, 0),
